          "path": "_m/d/j/v/w/sacred-heart-cultural-center-wp/sacred-heart-catholic-church-a.jpg",
          "filename": "Sacred Heart Catholic Church, Augusta, Georgia (7652252862).jpg",
          "caption": "Sacred Heart was a beautful Roman Catholic Church in downtown Augusta, Georgia. It was originally built to service the needs of the area's growing Irish Catholic population in the late 19th century. However, floods and wars led to a decline in the number of people living in the city's center. Thus, Sacred Heart held its last mass in 1971. \nKnox Ltd. restored Sacred Heart in 1987, and a nonprofit organization was formed to maintain the historic facility and to develop and promote cultural activities. Today, Sacred Heart Cultural Center is open for tours and is available for community events. \nAddress is below (church is geo mapped on this page)\n1301 Greene St.\n\nAugusta Georgia",
